# DEBRIS FALLING THROUGH THE SKY (21_falls, src/render/falls/), over the
# shoulder: each class staged on the bearing the view faces as it lights, at dusk -- the sun
# gone from the land but not from eighty kilometres up, so a train hangs gold --
# and again in the dark, where the trains are the moon's. Dust is a short
# streak; a fragment breaks up, its pieces diverging off the break with trains
# of their own; a mass burns high overhead, and the view tips up to follow it
# (21_falls `gaze`) and eases home.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/falls_sky.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=21.2 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0 --fall=dust@21.3,fragment@21.4,mass@21.75,dust@23.3,fragment@23.4,mass@23.75
wait 2
# The clock ran while the world warmed up; put it back before the first fall.
hour 21.25
await fall 10
shot 00-dusk-dust with fall
await fall_breakup 15
shot 01-dusk-fragment-breaking-up
wait 1.5
shot 02-dusk-fragment-pieces with fall
wait 5
shot 03-dusk-train with fall_train
until fall 25
mouse 0,-3000 1.2
await fall_breakup 15
shot 04-dusk-mass-overhead
wait 2
shot 05-dusk-mass-pieces with fall
# Once the pieces are out nothing holds the gaze: the view eases home by itself.
wait 9
hour 23.25
await fall 10
shot 10-night-dust with fall
await fall_breakup 15
shot 11-night-fragment-breaking-up
wait 1.5
shot 12-night-fragment-pieces with fall
wait 5
shot 13-night-train with fall_train
until fall 25
mouse 0,-3000 1.2
await fall_breakup 15
shot 14-night-mass-overhead
wait 2
shot 15-night-mass-pieces with fall
